# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_extractor_ecto.py" "ECTO GATE: PASS" "Ecto/Phoenix ORM extractor (schema macro + migration create/alter table)" "Ecto schema macro and migration macros now mint table nodes and alters/queries edges, lighting up the cross-substrate crown jewel for Phoenix/Elixir repos." "Adds Ecto/Phoenix ORM extraction to _cg_schema._ORM_PATTERNS so Phoenix apps no longer extract 0 table nodes. THE GAP FIXED: .ex/.exs were already walked (Elixir structural shipped in PR 293) but _ORM_PATTERNS had no Ecto patterns -- every Phoenix app produced 0 table nodes and the cross-substrate crown jewel (migration alters T + schema model queries T with NO import/call edge) was invisible for Elixir repos. TWO FORMS COVERED: (1) Ecto schema macro in model files: 'schema users do' anchored on the schema keyword followed immediately by a string literal (the exact table name). Precision: use Ecto.Schema / import Ecto.Schema / bare schema variable references do NOT match -- they lack the trailing string. (2) Ecto migration macros in priv/repo/migrations/.exs: 'create table(:name)' and 'alter table(:name)' for both the atom form ':name' (idiomatic Elixir, group 1) and the string form 'name' (group 2, rare but valid). Precision: create_table(:foo) (Rails) and .createTable( (Knex) are distinct tokens and do NOT match. _is_migration() already detects the migrations/ path segment so migration files correctly get alters edges. WHAT THIS GATE PROVES (hermetic, no DB, no Postgres, no network): (1) schema macro mints table node; (2) migration create table atom form mints table; (3) create table with extra options (primary_key: false) mints correctly -- options after the name do not interfere; (4) migration alter table atom form mints table; (5) string-literal create table form mints table; (6) CROSS-SUBSTRATE CROWN JEWEL: Ecto migration (priv/repo/migrations, alters edge) + Ecto schema model (lib, queries edge) are coupled via the shared table node with CONFIRMED absence of any calls/imports edge between them; (7) PRECISION: plain Elixir string not preceded by schema macro does NOT mint a table; (8) PRECISION: 'use Ecto.Schema' alone does NOT mint a table; (9) never-crash: empty .ex, malformed bytes, non-.ex files do not raise; (10) content-free: no file body or field values appear in the graph. MEASURED on papercups-io/papercups (real Phoenix/Ecto app): BEFORE 0 tables; AFTER 40 tables (accounts/conversations/customers/messages/users etc) with 130 alters edges and 46 queries edges; all 40 tables have both alters and queries edges confirming the cross-substrate coupling works end-to-end." 20
